      "exact_segment": "For each live C body or runtime program require its Rust implementation, focused\nbehavior/ABI checks, actual production selection/link ownership and applicable\nmatching native proof. Calling Linux/libc APIs through FFI is allowed; calling\nremaining project C implementation bodies is not final closure. Preserve current\nfunctional code until a successor passes. Do not change the pinned platform,\nresource limits or native execution authority through a source-only plan.\n\nFour final joins remain open: a complete delivered-runtime ownership manifest;\nactual C-free project module links under the pinned Rust-enabled kernel;\nRust executor/library/tool artifacts and their project dependency closure; and\nmatching module/application/lifecycle/resource-restoration behavior. Reuse matching\nexisting practical evidence and test the changed paths with the real new cohort.\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "/home/holden/mckernel/docs/verification/os-milestones-20260914/README.md",
      "lines": [
        640,
        651
      ],
      "segment_sha256": "a250f97dd622c6a80e52e2e2cfeeff9000bad152643a336d7f794d7d75ae81d0",
      "exact_segment": "## What the user needs to provide\n\n1. Available account quota and the local signed-in Codex CLI. Run the launcher;\n   it selects Sol/medium and Luna workers. No chat model change is required.\n2. Keep the workspace, retained scratch inputs and permitted container/runtime\n   access available. Begin with M00 storage and state checks.\n3. For later qualification, designate the required Intel/AMD systems and larger\n   virtual profiles, campaign capacity, permitted boot/rollback environments and\n   signing/release operator. Keep unavailable jobs explicitly blocked while\n   local work continues.\n4. Start or resume with the same launcher command; use `--status` and CURRENT. Review concise milestone outcomes and\n   escalations; there is no need to dispatch every individual worker yourself.\n"
    }
  ],
